			"config": {
				"register": "shillinq",
				"schema": "InventoryValuation",
				"_note": "VALUATION snapshot (the FIFO/AVG value of a product's stock at a warehouse on a date — the number that lands on the balance sheet and feeds COGS). The body foregrounds the valuation maths: quantity × unit cost = total value, the method that produced it, the date, warehouse, product and cost-center it books to, and the pending-COGS flag. A leaf snapshot with no child lines; no comms. The audit trail sidebar is the recalculation/method-change record, essential when a valuation is restated.",
